// STM32F407 — peripheral base-address table.
//
// 2026-08-03: flat .dbvl line-table (plan §5.1): one CAPITALIZED constant per
// line, `KEY: base_addr; size;`. Hex literals parse as String; the resolver
// radix-parses. This is the backing table for `address_resolver::resolve_address`
// (board map wins over config/address-map.toml and the hardcoded fallback).
//
// Sources: STM32F407xx datasheet §4.2 memory map; peripheral register
// addresses carried from the pre-v2 lib/boards/stm32f407.dbvl.

>schema Device from "map.dbv"
UART1: 0x40011000; 0x18;
UART2: 0x40004400; 0x18;
GPIOA: 0x40020000; 0x400;
GPIOB: 0x40020400; 0x400;
